---
components: ["CssGrid", "CssColumn"]
description: CssGrid is Carbon v11's CSS Grid layout mode, a display:grid alternative to the flexbox Grid with column spans, start/end placement, and percentage spans.
---

## Basic

`CssGrid` is Carbon v11's `display: grid` layout mode. It uses the same
breakpoints, column counts, gutters, and margins as the flexbox
[Grid](/components/Grid), but each `CssColumn` is a grid item placed directly
on the grid's tracks. No `Row` is needed: columns wrap onto a new row when the
current one is full.

Set a numeric `span` for a width that stays the same at every breakpoint.
Below, each column spans 4 tracks: the full row at `sm` (4 columns), half at
`md` (8 columns), and a quarter at `lg` and up (16 columns). `span={0}` hides
the column, and `span={true}` sizes it to its content (`grid-column: auto`).

<FileSource src="/framed/CssGrid/CssGrid" />

| Do | Why |
| --- | --- |
| Place `CssColumn` as a direct child of `CssGrid` | Only direct children are grid items. A wrapper element takes the column's track and the `CssColumn` inside it is laid out as a block |
| Use `CssGrid` when you need start/end placement or percentage spans | The flexbox `Grid` has neither. It only has spans and offsets |
| Stay with `Grid`/`Row`/`Column` in a layout that already uses them | The two modes do not mix: a `CssColumn` inside a `Row`, or a `Column` inside a `CssGrid`, is not sized by the grid around it |

## Spans

### Percentage

Set `span` to `"25%"`, `"50%"`, `"75%"`, or `"100%"` for a width relative to
the current column count. `"50%"` is 2 of 4 columns at `sm`, 4 of 8 at `md`,
and 8 of 16 at `lg` and up.

<FileSource src="/framed/CssGrid/CssGridPercent" />

### Responsive

Set `sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xlg`, or `max` to change the span per breakpoint. Each
breakpoint takes the same values as `span`: a number, a percentage, `true`, or
a descriptor object (see [Placement](#placement)). A value applies from its
breakpoint up until a larger breakpoint overrides it. `sm={0}` hides the last
column below `md`.

<FileSource src="/framed/CssGrid/CssGridResponsive" />

## Placement

Pass a descriptor object (`{ span, start, end, offset }`) to `span` or to a
breakpoint prop to place a column on specific grid lines. Grid lines are
numbered from 1, so a 16-column grid has lines 1 to 17.

### Start and end

`start` and `end` are grid line numbers. Combine `start` with `span` to set a
start line and a width, or `start` with `end` to set both edges. `start: 0`
resets to automatic placement.

<FileSource src="/framed/CssGrid/CssGridStartEnd" />

### Offset

`offset` is a column count, not a line number: `offset: 2` skips 2 columns and
starts the column on line 3. `offset: 0` resets to automatic placement. Set
either `offset` or `start`, not both: if both are set, both start lines are
applied and the higher one wins.

<FileSource src="/framed/CssGrid/CssGridOffset" />

## Variants

### Narrow

`narrow` removes the gutter on the leading side of each column, so column
content hangs into the gutter.

<FileSource src="/framed/CssGrid/NarrowCssGrid" />

### Condensed

`condensed` collapses the gutter to 1px, for dense layouts such as data
displays or image grids.

<FileSource src="/framed/CssGrid/CondensedCssGrid" />

### Row gap

`withRowGap` adds vertical space between rows equal to the gutter width. On a
`narrow` grid the row gap is halved to match.

<FileSource src="/framed/CssGrid/CssGridRowGap" />

## Subgrid

### Nested grid

Nest a `CssGrid` inside a `CssColumn` to split that column into its own grid.
The nested grid renders as a subgrid (`bx--subgrid`): it has one track per
column the parent spans, and it cancels the parent column's gutter so its
columns line up with the outer grid. Below, the subgrid's columns sit on the
same tracks as the outer columns in the next row.

<FileSource src="/framed/CssGrid/CssSubgrid" />

| Do | Why |
| --- | --- |
| Give the parent `CssColumn` a span at every breakpoint | The subgrid takes its track count from the parent's span. A parent with no span, or with `span={true}`, gives the subgrid the full grid's column count |
| Use numeric spans for columns inside a subgrid | Percentage spans resolve against the page grid's column count, not the subgrid's. `"50%"` at `lg` is 8 tracks even in a 12-track subgrid |
| Use `mode` on a nested `CssGrid`, not `narrow` or `condensed` | `narrow`, `condensed`, and `fullWidth` only apply to a top-level grid and are ignored on a subgrid |

### Modes

Without `mode`, a subgrid keeps the gutters of the grid around it. Set `mode`
to `"wide"`, `"narrow"`, or `"condensed"` to give the subgrid's columns their
own gutters: `wide` is the default 32px gutter, `narrow` removes the gutter on
the leading side, and `condensed` collapses it to 1px. `withRowGap` on a
subgrid adds a 32px row gap, 16px for `narrow` and 1px for `condensed`. `mode`
has no effect on a top-level grid.

<FileSource src="/framed/CssGrid/CssSubgridModes" />
